SwiftShell is a shell language that reads like code: variables, arrays, functions, loops, conditionals, pipelines and redirection, with real Unix commands.

The `swift` command is the front door, with dozens of subcommands and a curated offline package registry (`swift install hello`, `swift registry`, `swift search`). `swiftshell` is available as an alias.

To run the REPL: swift shell
To see every command: swift commands
